# Typography: Break long words new-line and same-line cut a word wider than its line, which is an error by default.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · Long words
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 30
			Vertical: top
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
		For style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 110
				Padding: 6
				Background: tint
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Long words
		Paragraph: An IBAN, an email address or a URL have no place to split, and in a narrow box they do not fit in a line. By default (`Break long words: never`) such a word is an error. With `new-line` or `same-line` it is cut at the last letter that fits, with no hyphen.
			Style: intro
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Break long words: new-line
						Style: label
					Paragraph: IBAN ES9121000418450200051332 of the supplier.
						Style: narrow
						Typography:
							Break long words: new-line
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Break long words: same-line
						Style: label
					Paragraph: IBAN ES9121000418450200051332 of the supplier.
						Style: narrow
						Typography:
							Break long words: same-line
		Text: A word that fits in a line of its own moves to the next line and is not cut
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Write to admin@nogal.example for the invoices.
			Style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 140
			Typography:
				Break long words: new-line
